    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d266-a3">

                <pb facs="0278" n="956" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg956"/>


                <head>Mr. Burlingame to Prince
                        Kung</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-06-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 26, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Permit me to thank your Imperial Highness
                    most cordially for extending the time in which to re-export native produce from
                    three months to one year. The change will do much to facilitate trade and to
                    strengthen the friendly relations already existing between our two
                    countries.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ANSON BURLINGAME.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Imperial Highness Prince <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kung</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chief Secretary of Foreign Affairs.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
